{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change pushed for review: **Gerrit 1684** — \"Add Markdown-aware Cloud ADF conversion\" (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1684). Awaiting `LLM-Review` and `Verified`. Rebased onto current origin/main immediately before pushing, so the base is fresh.\n\nPlan-review PASSED and signed in this environment before the claim (the six children's prior attestations were all `foreign_key`, signed under a different principal, so each needs re-earning here).\n\n## What landed in the change\n- `adapters/jira/adf.py` (+136) — `markdown_to_adf`, `adf_to_markdown`, `fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`, the `_canonicalize_marks` helper, and `plain_text_adf_functions()` (the whole-codec fallback set story 3388 installs).\n- `pyproject.toml` / `src/rebar/_optional.py` — the `adf` extra (`marklas==0.8.6`, `mistune==3.3.4`), pinned exactly, plus a dev pin so CI exercises the path rather than skipping. Registered in the `EXTRAS` registry.\n- `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py` + `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_{00,01,02}.json` — committed generator and 360-body scrubbed snapshot, largest shard 151 KB (under the 500 KB `check-added-large-files` cap).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_adf_markdown.py` (+190) — 12 tests covering all 12 ACs.\n- `uv.lock` regenerated — `uv lock --check` is a GATING CI step, so a stale lock would have been an automatic `Verified -1`.\n\n## Verification run locally\n- 44 tests pass in the new file plus the untouched `test_rich_text_codec.py`; the full `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` suite is green at **2,464 passed**.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` both green (514 files).\n- `test_optional.py` / `test_packaging_dependencies.py` / `test_core_optionality.py` green — these guard the stdlib-only engine contract the lazy-import design depends on.\n- Complexity baseline gate: `active=60 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n- `adf.py` is 499 lines, inside the 800-line module cap.\n\n## Evidence for the two engine defects\n- **Mark-order 2-cycle is eliminated.** Before: `A **~~both~~** end` alternated with `A ~~**both**~~ end` indefinitely. After sorting each text node's `marks` by type, the body is byte-stable across 5 consecutive round-trips.\n- **HTML comments now survive.** `markdown_to_adf` decodes its own output and, if a `<!-- … -->` present in the source went missing, returns the plain `text_to_adf` encode for that body instead. Exactly 1 of the 360 committed corpus bodies carries an HTML comment and loses it without this guard.\n\n## Corpus measurements (from the committed fixture, not the vanished export)\n360 bodies, 0 conversion errors; **100.00%** reach a fixed point after one pass (AC bar >=99.6%); **15.6%** are structurally rich under the explicit block-node predicate (AC bar >=15%); scrub verified — 0 tenant hostnames, 0 real emails, 0 live URLs.\n\nOne note for the cutover story: `AdfCodec` and all four of its ops are untouched here, and `test_adf_codec_is_a_pass_through_to_the_pinned_adf_module` stays green unmodified, so nothing observable changes on merge."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786573533296952001,"uuid":"b0be56cc-6c16-4f76-a3d5-e568d288532c"}